<section class="block">
  <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Three steps, no account needed to just look</h2>
  <div class="how-steps">
    <div class="how-step">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      <h3>Browse, free</h3>
      <p>See every listed event by city, state, date, and category &mdash; as a pinned-flyer list or a full 30-day calendar. No login required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      <h3>Check the calendar, then post</h3>
      <p>Pick your city and a full month view shows which days already have events booked. Listings start at $1; the $3 Standard listing stays live right up through the day of your event.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      <h3>Create a free account, get alerts</h3>
      <p>Sign up as a Viewer, pick your interests and area, and we'll let you know when something new matches.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Before you post</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>The board looks empty near me — is it worth checking?</summary>
      <p>Yes &mdash; even where no organizer has posted yet, NoClash is already pulling in public events from Ticketmaster and, for Hampton Roads cities, straight from each city's own events calendar (tagged <strong>Public Search</strong>). Pick your city on the <a href="/board">board</a> to see what's already scheduled before you add your own.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Why does posting cost $1 if Facebook Events is free?</summary>
      <p>A dollar keeps the board a curated, checked calendar instead of an open feed anyone can flood &mdash; and it pays for the conflict check that flags when another organizer already has your date and city. Browsing stays free either way.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Who is NoClash for?</summary>
      <p>Small-budget community organizers &mdash; PTAs, churches, nonprofits, neighborhood associations, school and civic groups. It's not built for professional event companies or venues running a packed commercial calendar. Read more on the <a href="/about">About</a> page.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Pick a listing tier, or go unlimited</h2>
  <div class="home-pricing-teaser">
    <div class="plan-card">
      <span class="tier">Per-Event Listings</span>
      <span class="price">$1&ndash;$5</span>
      <ul>
        <li>Standard ($3) stays live until the day of your event</li>
        <li>Edit anytime, add your link later</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="plan-card pass">
      <span class="tier">Organizer Pass</span>
      <span class="price">$49 <small>/ year</small></span>
      <ul>
        <li>Unlimited listings all year</li>
        <li>Priority email support</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">Free to browse, always &mdash; no credit card required. Edit or remove your listing anytime.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:14px;"><a class="btn-primary" href="/pricing">See full pricing &rarr;</a></p>
</section>

